# Jennifer is not a GitHub Linguist language yet. An override naming a language
# Linguist does not know is not a label but an exclusion: the .j files drop out
# of the statistics, and the language bar is left to the shell scripts around
# them (tools/*.sh). Without the override they are guessed as JASS / Objective-J
# instead.
#
# So nothing else is counted either, and the bar stays empty until Linguist
# learns Jennifer. The Jennifer line is already right for that day. A launcher
# with a jennifer shebang and no extension needs a line of its own:
#   bin/NAME linguist-language=Jennifer linguist-detectable=true
* linguist-detectable=false
*.j linguist-language=Jennifer linguist-detectable=true
